Close a TCP connection whose read side failed while a partial answer is buffered.

c-ares 1.34.7 (c-ares/c-ares#1138) stopped closing a connection at once when
a read fails while data is buffered. read_conn_packets() sets conn_error and
process_read() is meant to close the connection after read_answers() has
parsed what was buffered.

That close is unreachable. The loop in read_answers() only ends when
ares_buf_fetch_be16() or ares_buf_consume() runs out of data, which leaves
status as ARES_EBADRESP, so process_read() always takes the early return
before it looks at conn_error.

When a DNS server sends part of a TCP frame and closes, the connection stays
the server's tcp_conn until the query times out. The socket stays readable
(EOF), so a level-triggered poll wakes up on every loop iteration and each
recv() returns 0. Retries of the query are also written to the dead
connection. 1.34.6 failed the same query with ECONNREFUSED at once.

This patch moves the deferred close into read_answers(), between the parse
loop and the requeue flush. The connection is known to be alive there
(process_answer() never closes it), so no lookup by fd is needed after
callbacks have run, and retries flushed afterwards open a new connection.

--- a/src/lib/ares_process.c
+++ b/src/lib/ares_process.c
@@ -674,7 +674,8 @@
   return status;
 }
 
-static ares_status_t read_answers(ares_conn_t *conn, const ares_timeval_t *now)
+static ares_status_t read_answers(ares_conn_t *conn, ares_bool_t conn_error,
+                                  const ares_timeval_t *now)
 {
   ares_status_t   status;
   ares_channel_t *channel  = conn->server->channel;
@@ -725,6 +726,14 @@
     ares_buf_tag_clear(conn->in_buf);
   }
 
+  /* Bun: read_conn_packets() saw the connection fail with data still buffered
+   * and deferred the close to here.  Close before the flush so retries go to
+   * a new connection, and do not key this off status: the loop above always
+   * ends with a failure status once the buffer runs out. */
+  if (conn_error) {
+    handle_conn_error(conn, ARES_TRUE, ARES_ECONNREFUSED);
+  }
+
 cleanup:
   /* Flush requeue - re-dispatch retries and invoke deferred callbacks
    * iteratively and safely */
@@ -753,19 +762,7 @@
     return status;
   }
 
-  status = read_answers(conn, now);
-  if (status != ARES_SUCCESS) {
-    return status;
-  }
-
-  if (conn_error) {
-    conn = ares_conn_from_fd(channel, read_fd);
-    if (conn != NULL) {
-      handle_conn_error(conn, ARES_TRUE, ARES_ECONNREFUSED);
-    }
-  }
-
-  return ARES_SUCCESS;
+  return read_answers(conn, conn_error, now);
 }
 
 /* If any queries have timed out, note the timeout and move them on. */
